{"surah": 60, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ لَا تَتَّخِذُوا۟ عَدُوِّى وَعَدُوَّكُمْ أَوْلِيَآءَ تُلْقُونَ إِلَيْهِم بِٱلْمَوَدَّةِ وَقَدْ كَفَرُوا۟ بِمَا جَآءَكُم مِّنَ ٱلْحَقِّ يُخْرِجُونَ ٱلرَّسُولَ وَإِيَّاكُمْۙ أَن تُؤْمِنُوا۟ بِٱللَّهِ رَبِّكُمْ إِن كُنتُمْ خَرَجْتُمْ جِهَٰدًا فِى سَبِيلِى وَٱبْتِغَآءَ مَرْضَاتِىۚ تُسِرُّونَ إِلَيْهِم بِٱلْمَوَدَّةِ وَأَنَا۠ أَعْلَمُ بِمَآ أَخْفَيْتُمْ وَمَآ أَعْلَنتُمْۚ وَمَن يَفْعَلْهُ مِنكُمْ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ سَوَآءَ ٱلسَّبِيلِ ", "translation": "O you who have believed, do not take My enemies and your enemies as allies,[1] extending to them affection while they have disbelieved in what came to you of the truth, having driven out the Prophet and yourselves [only] because you believe in Allāh, your Lord. If you have come out for jihād [i.e., fighting or striving] in My cause and seeking means to My approval, [take them not as friends]. You confide to them affection [i.e., instruction], but I am most knowing of what you have concealed and what you have declared. And whoever does it among you has certainly strayed from the soundness of the way.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَتَّخِذُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُhdِhkَّtَt", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَدُوِّى", "translit": "àِّwُdَʿع", "root": "عدو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَعَدُوَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّwُdَʿعَw", "root": "عدو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَوْلِيَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَyِlْwَaʾ", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "تُلْقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqْlُt", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِم", "translit": "mِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِٱلْمَوَدَّةِ", "translit": "ِẗَّdَwَmْlٱِb", "root": "ودد"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "جَآءَكُم", "translit": "mُkَءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "يُخْرِجُونَ", "translit": "َnwُjgِrْhkُy", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلرَّسُولَ", "translit": "َlwُsَّrlٱ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَإِيَّاكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkāَّyِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "تُؤْمِنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnِmْwʾُt", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "بِٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱِb", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "رَبِّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "خَرَجْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْjgَrَhk", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "جِهَٰدًا", "translit": "āًdَٰhِjg", "root": "جهد"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "سَبِيلِى", "translit": "àِlyِbَs", "root": "سبل"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "وَٱبْتِغَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَغِtْbٱَw", "root": "بغي"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "مَرْضَاتِى", "translit": "àِtāَḍْrَm", "root": "رضو"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "تُسِرُّونَ", "translit": "َnwُّrِsُt", "root": "سرر"}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِم", "translit": "mِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "بِٱلْمَوَدَّةِ", "translit": "ِẗَّdَwَmْlٱِb", "root": "ودد"}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "وَأَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "أَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَaʾ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "بِمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 39, "arabic": "أَخْفَيْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْyَfْhkَaʾ", "root": "خفي"}, {"id": 40, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 41, "arabic": "أَعْلَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَlْʿعَaʾ", "root": "علن"}, {"id": 42, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 43, "arabic": "يَفْعَلْهُ", "translit": "ُhْlَʿعْfَy", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 44, "arabic": "مِنكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُknِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 45, "arabic": "فَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 46, "arabic": "ضَلَّ", "translit": "َّlَḍ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 47, "arabic": "سَوَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَwَs", "root": "سوي"}, {"id": 48, "arabic": "ٱلسَّبِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِbَّslٱ", "root": "سبل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "إِن يَثْقَفُوكُمْ يَكُونُوا۟ لَكُمْ أَعْدَآءً وَيَبْسُطُوٓا۟ إِلَيْكُمْ أَيْدِيَهُمْ وَأَلْسِنَتَهُم بِٱلسُّوٓءِ وَوَدُّوا۟ لَوْ تَكْفُرُونَ ", "translation": "If they gain dominance over you, they would be [i.e., behave] to you as enemies and extend against you their hands and their tongues with evil, and they wish you would disbelieve.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَثْقَفُوكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkwُfَqْhtَy", "root": "ثقف"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَكُونُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnwُkَy", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَعْدَآءً", "translit": "ًءٓāَdْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عدو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَيَبْسُطُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُṭُsْbَyَw", "root": "بسط"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِلَيْكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَيْدِيَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَyِdْyَaʾ", "root": "يدي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَأَلْسِنَتَهُم", "translit": "mُhَtَnِsْlَaʾَw", "root": "لسن"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "بِٱلسُّوٓءِ", "translit": "ِءٓwُّslٱِb", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَوَدُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّdَwَw", "root": "ودد"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَوْ", "translit": "ْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "تَكْفُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُfْkَt", "root": "كفر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "لَن تَنفَعَكُمْ أَرْحَامُكُمْ وَلَآ أَوْلَٰدُكُمْۚ يَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ يَفْصِلُ بَيْنَكُمْۚ وَٱللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ ", "translation": "Never will your relatives or your children benefit you; the Day of Resurrection He will judge between you. And Allāh, of what you do, is Seeing.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَن", "translit": "nَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَنفَعَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَʿعَfnَt", "root": "نفع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَرْحَامُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُmāَḥْrَaʾ", "root": "رحم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَوْلَٰدُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُdَٰlْwَaʾ", "root": "ولد"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَmَٰyِqْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَفْصِلُ", "translit": "ُlِṣْfَy", "root": "فصل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بَيْنَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "تَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْʿعَt", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "بَصِيرٌ", "translit": "ٌryِṣَb", "root": "بصر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "قَدْ كَانَتْ لَكُمْ أُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ فِىٓ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ وَٱلَّذِينَ مَعَهُۥٓ إِذْ قَالُوا۟ لِقَوْمِهِمْ إِنَّا بُرَءَٰٓؤُا۟ مِنكُمْ وَمِمَّا تَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ كَفَرْنَا بِكُمْ وَبَدَا بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمُ ٱلْعَدَٰوَةُ وَٱلْبَغْضَآءُ أَبَدًا حَتَّىٰ تُؤْمِنُوا۟ بِٱللَّهِ وَحْدَهُۥٓ إِلَّا قَوْلَ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ لِأَبِيهِ لَأَسْتَغْفِرَنَّ لَكَ وَمَآ أَمْلِكُ لَكَ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ مِن شَىْءٍۖ رَّبَّنَا عَلَيْكَ تَوَكَّلْنَا وَإِلَيْكَ أَنَبْنَا وَإِلَيْكَ ٱلْمَصِيرُ ", "translation": "There has already been for you an excellent pattern[1] in Abraham and those with him, when they said to their people, \"Indeed, we are disassociated from you and from whatever you worship other than Allāh. We have denied you, and there has appeared between us and you animosity and hatred forever until you believe in Allāh alone\" - except for the saying of Abraham to his father, \"I will surely ask forgiveness for you, but I have not [power to do] for you anything against Allāh. Our Lord, upon You we have relied, and to You we have returned, and to You is the destination.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَتْ", "translit": "ْtَnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أُسْوَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَwْsُaʾ", "root": "اسو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "حَسَنَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَnَsَḥ", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِبْرَٰهِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِhَٰrْbِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَعَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لِقَوْمِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِmْwَqِl", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "بُرَءَٰٓؤُا۟", "translit": "۟āُwʾَٰٓءَrُb", "root": "برا"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مِنكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُknِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَمِمَّا", "translit": "āَّmِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "تَعْبُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُbْʿعَt", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "دُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "كَفَرْنَا", "translit": "āَnْrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "بِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "وَبَدَا", "translit": "āَdَbَw", "root": "بدو"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "بَيْنَنَا", "translit": "āَnَnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "وَبَيْنَكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkَnْyَbَw", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ٱلْعَدَٰوَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَwَٰdَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عدو"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "وَٱلْبَغْضَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَḍْغَbْlٱَw", "root": "بغض"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "أَبَدًا", "translit": "āًdَbَaʾ", "root": "ابد"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "تُؤْمِنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnِmْwʾُt", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "بِٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱِb", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "وَحْدَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَdْḥَw", "root": "وحد"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "قَوْلَ", "translit": "َlْwَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "إِبْرَٰهِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِhَٰrْbِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "لِأَبِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِbَaʾِl", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "لَأَسْتَغْفِرَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَrِfْغَtْsَaʾَl", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "لَكَ", "translit": "َkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 39, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 40, "arabic": "أَمْلِكُ", "translit": "ُkِlْmَaʾ", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 41, "arabic": "لَكَ", "translit": "َkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 42, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 43, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 44, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 45, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 46, "arabic": "رَّبَّنَا", "translit": "āَnَّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 47, "arabic": "عَلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 48, "arabic": "تَوَكَّلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَّkَwَt", "root": "وكل"}, {"id": 49, "arabic": "وَإِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 50, "arabic": "أَنَبْنَا", "translit": "āَnْbَnَaʾ", "root": "نوب"}, {"id": 51, "arabic": "وَإِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 52, "arabic": "ٱلْمَصِيرُ", "translit": "ُryِṣَmْlٱ", "root": "صير"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "رَبَّنَا لَا تَجْعَلْنَا فِتْنَةً لِّلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ وَٱغْفِرْ لَنَا رَبَّنَآۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلْحَكِيمُ ", "translation": "Our Lord, make us not [objects of] torment for the disbelievers and forgive us, our Lord. Indeed, it is You who is the Exalted in Might, the Wise.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "رَبَّنَا", "translit": "āَnَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَجْعَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَʿعْjgَt", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِتْنَةً", "translit": "ًẗَnْtِf", "root": "فتن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لِّلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَٱغْفِرْ", "translit": "ْrِfْغٱَw", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَنَا", "translit": "āَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "رَبَّنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِنَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزُ", "translit": "ُzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلْحَكِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِkَḥْlٱ", "root": "حكم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "لَقَدْ كَانَ لَكُمْ فِيهِمْ أُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ لِّمَن كَانَ يَرْجُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَٱلْيَوْمَ ٱلْءَاخِرَۚ وَمَن يَتَوَلَّ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ هُوَ ٱلْغَنِىُّ ٱلْحَمِيدُ ", "translation": "There has certainly been for you in them an excellent pattern for anyone whose hope is in Allāh and the Last Day. And whoever turns away - then indeed, Allāh is the Free of need, the Praiseworthy.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِيهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أُسْوَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَwْsُaʾ", "root": "اسو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "حَسَنَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَnَsَḥ", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لِّمَن", "translit": "nَmِّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَرْجُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُjgْrَy", "root": "رجو"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَٱلْيَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَyْlٱَw", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرَ", "translit": "َrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَتَوَلَّ", "translit": "َّlَwَtَy", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلْغَنِىُّ", "translit": "ُّàِnَغْlٱ", "root": "غني"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلْحَمِيدُ", "translit": "ُdyِmَḥْlٱ", "root": "حمد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "عَسَى ٱللَّهُ أَن يَجْعَلَ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَ ٱلَّذِينَ عَادَيْتُم مِّنْهُم مَّوَدَّةًۚ وَٱللَّهُ قَدِيرٌۚ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ ", "translation": "Perhaps Allāh will put, between you and those to whom you have been enemies among them, affection. And Allāh is competent,[1] and Allāh is Forgiving and Merciful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "عَسَى", "translit": "àَsَʿع", "root": "عسي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَجْعَلَ", "translit": "َlَʿعْjgَy", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بَيْنَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَبَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَbَw", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَادَيْتُم", "translit": "mُtْyَdāَʿع", "root": "عدو"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِّنْهُم", "translit": "mُhْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مَّوَدَّةً", "translit": "ًẗَّdَwَّm", "root": "ودد"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "قَدِيرٌ", "translit": "ٌryِdَq", "root": "قدر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "غَفُورٌ", "translit": "ٌrwُfَغ", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "رَّحِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِḥَّr", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "لَّا يَنْهَىٰكُمُ ٱللَّهُ عَنِ ٱلَّذِينَ لَمْ يُقَٰتِلُوكُمْ فِى ٱلدِّينِ وَلَمْ يُخْرِجُوكُم مِّن دِيَٰرِكُمْ أَن تَبَرُّوهُمْ وَتُقْسِطُوٓا۟ إِلَيْهِمْۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُحِبُّ ٱلْمُقْسِطِينَ ", "translation": "Allāh does not forbid you from those who do not fight you because of religion and do not expel you from your homes - from being righteous toward them and acting justly toward them. Indeed, Allāh loves those who act justly.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَنْهَىٰكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkٰàَhْnَy", "root": "نهي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَنِ", "translit": "ِnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَمْ", "translit": "ْmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يُقَٰتِلُوكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkwُlِtَٰqُy", "root": "قتل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلدِّينِ", "translit": "ِnyِّdlٱ", "root": "دين"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يُخْرِجُوكُم", "translit": "mُkwُjgِrْhkُy", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "دِيَٰرِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِrَٰyِd", "root": "دور"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "تَبَرُّوهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhwُّrَbَt", "root": "برر"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَتُقْسِطُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُṭِsْqُtَw", "root": "قسط"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "يُحِبُّ", "translit": "ُّbِḥُy", "root": "حبب"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "ٱلْمُقْسِطِينَ", "translit": "َnyِṭِsْqُmْlٱ", "root": "قسط"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "إِنَّمَا يَنْهَىٰكُمُ ٱللَّهُ عَنِ ٱلَّذِينَ قَٰتَلُوكُمْ فِى ٱلدِّينِ وَأَخْرَجُوكُم مِّن دِيَٰرِكُمْ وَظَٰهَرُوا۟ عَلَىٰٓ إِخْرَاجِكُمْ أَن تَوَلَّوْهُمْۚ وَمَن يَتَوَلَّهُمْ فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ ", "translation": "Allāh only forbids you from those who fight you because of religion and expel you from your homes and aid in your expulsion - [forbids] that you make allies[1] of them. And whoever makes allies of them, then it is those who are the wrongdoers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّمَا", "translit": "āَmَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَنْهَىٰكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkٰàَhْnَy", "root": "نهي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَنِ", "translit": "ِnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قَٰتَلُوكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkwُlَtَٰq", "root": "قتل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلدِّينِ", "translit": "ِnyِّdlٱ", "root": "دين"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَأَخْرَجُوكُم", "translit": "mُkwُjgَrْhkَaʾَw", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "دِيَٰرِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِrَٰyِd", "root": "دور"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَظَٰهَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَhَٰẓَw", "root": "ظهر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِخْرَاجِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِjgāَrْhkِiʾ", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "تَوَلَّوْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْwَّlَwَt", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "يَتَوَلَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّlَwَtَy", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "هُمُ", "translit": "ُmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmِlَّٰẓlٱ", "root": "ظلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓا۟ إِذَا جَآءَكُمُ ٱلْمُؤْمِنَٰتُ مُهَٰجِرَٰتٍ فَٱمْتَحِنُوهُنَّۖ ٱللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِإِيمَٰنِهِنَّۖ فَإِنْ عَلِمْتُمُوهُنَّ مُؤْمِنَٰتٍ فَلَا تَرْجِعُوهُنَّ إِلَى ٱلْكُفَّارِۖ لَا هُنَّ حِلٌّ لَّهُمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحِلُّونَ لَهُنَّۖ وَءَاتُوهُم مَّآ أَنفَقُوا۟ۚ وَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ أَن تَنكِحُوهُنَّ إِذَآ ءَاتَيْتُمُوهُنَّ أُجُورَهُنَّۚ وَلَا تُمْسِكُوا۟ بِعِصَمِ ٱلْكَوَافِرِ وَسْـَٔلُوا۟ مَآ أَنفَقْتُمْ وَلْيَسْـَٔلُوا۟ مَآ أَنفَقُوا۟ۚ ذَٰلِكُمْ حُكْمُ ٱللَّهِۖ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَكُمْۚ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ ", "translation": "O you who have believed, when the believing women come to you as emigrants, examine [i.e., test] them. Allāh is most knowing as to their faith. And if you know them to be believers, then do not return them to the disbelievers; they are not lawful [wives] for them, nor are they lawful [husbands] for them. But give them [i.e., the disbelievers] what they have spent.[1] And there is no blame upon you if you marry them when you have given them their due compensation [i.e., mahr]. And hold not to marriage bonds with disbelieving women, but ask for what you have spent and let them [i.e., the disbelievers] ask for what they have spent.[2] That is the judgement of Allāh; He judges between you. And Allāh is Knowing and Wise.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "جَآءَكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkَءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْمُؤْمِنَٰتُ", "translit": "ُtَٰnِmْwʾُmْlٱ", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مُهَٰجِرَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰrِjgَٰhُm", "root": "هجر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَٱمْتَحِنُوهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhwُnِḥَtْmٱَf", "root": "محن"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَaʾ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِإِيمَٰنِهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhِnَٰmyِiʾِb", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فَإِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَلِمْتُمُوهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhwُmُtْmِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مُؤْمِنَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰnِmْwʾُm", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "تَرْجِعُوهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhwُʿعِjgْrَt", "root": "رجع"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلْكُفَّارِ", "translit": "ِrāَّfُkْlٱ", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "هُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "حِلٌّ", "translit": "ٌّlِḥ", "root": "حلل"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "لَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "هُمْ", "translit": "ْmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "يَحِلُّونَ", "translit": "َnwُّlِḥَy", "root": "حلل"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "لَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "وَءَاتُوهُم", "translit": "mُhwُtāَءَw", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "مَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "أَنفَقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَfnَaʾ", "root": "نفق"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "جُنَاحَ", "translit": "َḥāَnُjg", "root": "جنح"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "عَلَيْكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "تَنكِحُوهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhwُḥِknَt", "root": "نكح"}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "إِذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "ءَاتَيْتُمُوهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhwُmُtْyَtāَء", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "أُجُورَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَrwُjgُaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 39, "arabic": "تُمْسِكُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُkِsْmُt", "root": "مسك"}, {"id": 40, "arabic": "بِعِصَمِ", "translit": "ِmَṣِʿعِb", "root": "عصم"}, {"id": 41, "arabic": "ٱلْكَوَافِرِ", "translit": "ِrِfāَwَkْlٱ", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 42, "arabic": "وَسْـَٔلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَٔـْsَw", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 43, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 44, "arabic": "أَنفَقْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْqَfnَaʾ", "root": "نفق"}, {"id": 45, "arabic": "وَلْيَسْـَٔلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَٔـْsَyْlَw", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 46, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 47, "arabic": "أَنفَقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَfnَaʾ", "root": "نفق"}, {"id": 48, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 49, "arabic": "حُكْمُ", "translit": "ُmْkُḥ", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 50, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 51, "arabic": "يَحْكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkْḥَy", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 52, "arabic": "بَيْنَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 53, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 54, "arabic": "عَلِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 55, "arabic": "حَكِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِkَḥ", "root": "حكم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "وَإِن فَاتَكُمْ شَىْءٌ مِّنْ أَزْوَٰجِكُمْ إِلَى ٱلْكُفَّارِ فَعَاقَبْتُمْ فَـَٔاتُوا۟ ٱلَّذِينَ ذَهَبَتْ أَزْوَٰجُهُم مِّثْلَ مَآ أَنفَقُوا۟ۚ وَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ ٱلَّذِىٓ أَنتُم بِهِۦ مُؤْمِنُونَ ", "translation": "And if you have lost any of your wives to the disbelievers and you subsequently obtain [something],[1] then give those whose wives have gone the equivalent of what they had spent. And fear Allāh, in whom you are believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَاتَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَtāَf", "root": "فوت"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "شَىْءٌ", "translit": "ٌءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَزْوَٰجِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِjgَٰwْzَaʾ", "root": "زوج"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْكُفَّارِ", "translit": "ِrāَّfُkْlٱ", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَعَاقَبْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْbَqāَʿعَf", "root": "عقب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فَـَٔاتُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُtāَٔـَf", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ذَهَبَتْ", "translit": "ْtَbَhَhd", "root": "ذهب"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَزْوَٰجُهُم", "translit": "mُhُjgَٰwْzَaʾ", "root": "زوج"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مِّثْلَ", "translit": "َlْhtِّm", "root": "مثل"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "أَنفَقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَfnَaʾ", "root": "نفق"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَw", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "أَنتُم", "translit": "mُtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "مُؤْمِنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnِmْwʾُm", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِىُّ إِذَا جَآءَكَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنَٰتُ يُبَايِعْنَكَ عَلَىٰٓ أَن لَّا يُشْرِكْنَ بِٱللَّهِ شَيْـًٔا وَلَا يَسْرِقْنَ وَلَا يَزْنِينَ وَلَا يَقْتُلْنَ أَوْلَٰدَهُنَّ وَلَا يَأْتِينَ بِبُهْتَٰنٍ يَفْتَرِينَهُۥ بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِنَّ وَأَرْجُلِهِنَّ وَلَا يَعْصِينَكَ فِى مَعْرُوفٍۙ فَبَايِعْهُنَّ وَٱسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُنَّ ٱللَّهَۖ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ ", "translation": "O Prophet, when the believing women come to you pledging to you that they will not associate anything with Allāh, nor will they steal, nor will they commit unlawful sexual intercourse, nor will they kill their children, nor will they bring forth a slander they have invented between their arms and legs,[1] nor will they disobey you in what is right - then accept their pledge and ask forgiveness for them of Allāh. Indeed, Allāh is Forgiving and Merciful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلنَّبِىُّ", "translit": "ُّàِbَّnlٱ", "root": "نبا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "جَآءَكَ", "translit": "َkَءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُؤْمِنَٰتُ", "translit": "ُtَٰnِmْwʾُmْlٱ", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يُبَايِعْنَكَ", "translit": "َkَnْʿعِyāَbُy", "root": "بيع"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يُشْرِكْنَ", "translit": "َnْkِrْhsُy", "root": "شرك"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱِb", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "شَيْـًٔا", "translit": "āًٔـْyَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَسْرِقْنَ", "translit": "َnْqِrْsَy", "root": "سرق"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَزْنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnْzَy", "root": "زني"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "يَقْتُلْنَ", "translit": "َnْlُtْqَy", "root": "قتل"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "أَوْلَٰدَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَdَٰlْwَaʾ", "root": "ولد"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "يَأْتِينَ", "translit": "َnyِtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "بِبُهْتَٰنٍ", "translit": "ٍnَٰtْhُbِb", "root": "بهت"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "يَفْتَرِينَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَnyِrَtْfَy", "root": "فري"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "بَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "أَيْدِيهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhyِdْyَaʾ", "root": "يدي"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "وَأَرْجُلِهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhِlُjgْrَaʾَw", "root": "رجل"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "يَعْصِينَكَ", "translit": "َkَnyِṣْʿعَy", "root": "عصي"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "مَعْرُوفٍ", "translit": "ٍfwُrْʿعَm", "root": "عرف"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "فَبَايِعْهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhْʿعِyāَbَf", "root": "بيع"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "وَٱسْتَغْفِرْ", "translit": "ْrِfْغَtْsٱَw", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "لَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "غَفُورٌ", "translit": "ٌrwُfَغ", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "رَّحِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِḥَّr", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ لَا تَتَوَلَّوْا۟ قَوْمًا غَضِبَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ قَدْ يَئِسُوا۟ مِنَ ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ كَمَا يَئِسَ ٱلْكُفَّارُ مِنْ أَصْحَٰبِ ٱلْقُبُورِ ", "translation": "O you who have believed, do not make allies of a people with whom Allāh has become angry. They have despaired of [reward in] the Hereafter just as the disbelievers have despaired of [meeting] the companions [i.e., inhabitants] of the graves.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَتَوَلَّوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَّlَwَtَt", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قَوْمًا", "translit": "āًmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "غَضِبَ", "translit": "َbِḍَغ", "root": "غضب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يَئِسُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُsِyʾَy", "root": "ياس"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "كَمَا", "translit": "āَmَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يَئِسَ", "translit": "َsِyʾَy", "root": "ياس"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْكُفَّارُ", "translit": "ُrāَّfُkْlٱ", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "أَصْحَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰḥْṣَaʾ", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلْقُبُورِ", "translit": "ِrwُbُqْlٱ", "root": "قبر"}], "hasIhya": true}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "وقد قال الله تعالى يا أيها الذين آمنوا أنفقوا من طيبات ما كسبتم ومما أخرجنا لكم من الأرض ولا تيمموا الخبيث منه تنفقون ولستم بآخذيه إلا أن تغمضوا فيه أي لا تأخذوه إلا مع كراهية وحياء وهو معنى الإغماض فلا تؤثروا به ربكم وفي الخبر سبق درهم مائة ألف درهم (3) وذلك بأن يخرجه الإنسان وهو من أحل ماله وأجوده فيصدر ذلك عن الرضا والفرح بالبذل وقد يخرج مائة ألف درهم مما يكره من ماله فيدل ذلك على أنه ليس يؤثر الله عز وجل بشيء مما يحبه وبذلك ذم الله تعالى قوما جعلوا لله ما يكرهون فقال تعال", "english": "The heart is not treated save with the compound electuary (maʿjūn) of knowledge and works. And this condition among the conditions of almsgiving runs in the same course as humility (al-khushūʿ) runs in the prayer. This is established by his saying — may Allah bless him and grant him peace: \"A man has nothing of his prayer save that of which he was conscious.\" And this is like his saying — may Allah bless him and grant him peace: \"Allah does not accept the charity of the one who bestows it with reproach (al-mannān).\" And like His saying — Exalted is He: {«لا تبطلوا صدقاتكم بالمن والأذى»} (\"Do not nullify your charities by reproach and injury\"). As for the legal opinion (fatwā) of the jurist that the alms fall in their proper place and that one's liability is discharged without this condition — that is another discussion, and we have already pointed to its meaning in the Book of Prayer.", "book_title": "Duties of Brotherhood", "section_title_ar": "Section 175", "section_title_en": "The Inner Conditions of Charity — Section 175 (From The Revival of the Religious Sciences, Book of the Mysteries of Almsgiving)", "section_index": 175, "anchors": "- Root: قلب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"To turn, overturn, transform a thing from one state to another; to rotate, to flip\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — the heart is so named because of its constant turning and transformation between states\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه\" (to turn a thing from its face). Metaphorical: \"رجل قلب حول: يقلب الأمور ويحتال\" — one who turns matters over and manages them; \"قلبوا لك الأمور\" (they turned matters against you)\n- Root: وجل (w-j-l)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Fear, dread, apprehension that strikes the heart\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف\" — the sensing of fear; cited in {«إنما المؤمنون الذين إذا ذكر الله وجلت قلوبهم»}\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"رجل وجل، وقوم وجال\" — a fearful man, a fearful people; \"وفي قلبه وجل\" — in his heart is dread\n- Root: عجب (ʿ-j-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Wonder, amazement; self-admiration, vanity\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Self-admiration (al-ʿujb) is a destructive spiritual ailment that nullifies deeds\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: wonder at something extraordinary. Metaphorical: self-conceit regarding one's own acts of obedience\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction & Focused Predication) — governing the precise limitation of general categories (al-ṣifāt al-khāṣṣah within al-aṣnāf al-thamāniyyah) and the conditional structure of acceptance\n\n---\n\n##", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Duties of Brotherhood'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وقال عز وجل {يا أيها الذين آمنوا لا تتخذوا عدوي وعدوكم أولياء} الآية الثاني المبتدع الذي يدعو إلى بدعته فإن كانت البدعة بحيث يكفر بها فأمره أشد من الذمي لأنه لا يقر بجزية ولا يسامح بعقد ذمة وإن كان ممن لا يكفر به فأمره بينه وبين الله أخف من أمر الكافر لا محالة ولكن الأمر في الإنكار عليه أشد منه على الكافر لأن شر الكافر غير متعد فإن المسلمين اعتقدوا كفره فلا يلتفتون إلى قوله إذ لا يدعي لنفسه الإسلام واعتقاد الحق أما المبتدع الذي يدعوا إلا البدعة ويزعم أن ما يدعو إليه حق فهو سبب لغواية الخلق فشره متعد فال", "english": "If you say: \"The manifestation of hatred and enmity by deed, even if not obligatory, is undoubtedly commendable (mandūb); yet the disobedient and the flagrant sinners are of varying ranks — so how is excellence attained by dealing with them, and is a single course pursued with all of them or not?\" — Know that the one who opposes the command of God, may He be exalted, is either one who opposes in his creed (ʿaqd) or in his deed (ʿamal). The one who opposes in creed is either an innovator (mubtadiʿ) or a disbeliever (kāfir). The innovator is either one who calls to his innovation (dāʿī) or one who remains silent — and the silent one is either so by incapacity or by choice. The divisions of corruption in belief are thus three:", "book_title": "Duties of Brotherhood", "section_title_ar": "Section 412", "section_title_en": "Exposition of the Ranks of Those Who Are Hated for God's Sake and the Manner of Dealing with Them", "section_index": 412, "anchors": "- Root: ب غ ض (b-gh-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of hatred and aversion, the opposite of love (al-ḥubb); al-baghḍāʾ is intense hatred.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — hatred for God's sake (al-bughḍ fī Allāh) is a spiritual act of the heart (laṭīfah rabbāniyyah) distinguishing sincere faith from hypocrisy.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) — aversion of the heart; metaphorical (majāz) — manifesting aversion through outward acts of avoidance and censure.\n- Root: ع ص و (ʿ-ṣ-w)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: ʿiṣyān — disobedience and rebellion against a command; the ʿāṣī is one who transgresses the bound.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — fisq (flagrant sin) is the departure from the straight path (khurūj ʿan al-ṭarīqah al-mustaqīmah) through willful transgression.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — breaking a command; metaphorical — persistence in sin without repentance.\n- Root: ب د ع (b-d-ʿ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: bidʿah — an innovation, a newly invented matter in religion without precedent.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — al-ibdāʿ is creation without model; for God it is bringing into being without instrument, matter, time, or place. For man, bidʿah is introducing into religion what is not from it.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — inventing something new; metaphorical — a weak argument (abdaʿat ḥujjatuka) or failing expectation.\n- Root: ك ف ر (k-f-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: kufr — covering, concealing; the night is called kāfir for covering persons; the farmer (kāfir) covers the seed.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — kufr is disbelief, the covering of truth; the kāfir is one who veils the truth of God's unity.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — covering (satar); metaphorical — ingratitude and rejection of divine blessings.\n- Root: ق ل ب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: qalb — the heart; taqallub — turning and changing from one state to another.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — the heart's fluctuation (taqallub al-qulūb) between states of faith and heedlessness; the hearts of the common folk are quick to turn.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — turning a thing over; metaphorical — the instability of opinion and disposition.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Conditional Partitioning (Taqsīm al-Sharṭ) — the division of a genus into exhaustive species governed by conditional clauses (in kāna... fa-), each branch receiving its own ruling without conflation.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Duties of Brotherhood'", "badge": "Insight"}], "4": [{"arabic": "حسنة وفي الآخرة إنا هدنا إليك ربنا عليك توكلنا وإليك أنبنا وإليك المصير ربنا لا تجعلنا فتنة للقوم الظالمين ربنا لا تجعلنا فتنة للذين كفروا واغفر لنا ربنا إنك أنت العزيز الحكيم ربنا اغفر لنا ذنوبنا وإسرافنا في أمرنا وثبت أقدامنا وانصرنا على القوم الكافرين ربنا اغفر لنا ولإخواننا الذين سبقونا بالإيمان ولا تجعل في قلوبنا غلا للذين آمنوا ربنا إنك رؤوف رحيم ربنا آتنا من لدنك رحمة وهيئ لنا من أمرنا رشدا ربنا آتنا في الدنيا حسنة وفي الآخرة حسنة وقنا عذاب النار ربنا إننا سمعنا مناديا ينادي للإيمان إلى قوله عز وجل إنك لا تخلف الميعاد ربنا لا تؤاخذنا إن نسينا أو أخطأنا ربنا إلى آخر السورة (3) رب اغفر لي ولوالدي وارحمهما كما ربيان", "english": "And employ me in righteous deeds which You will accept from me. (1) O God, I ask You for pardon, well-being, good certainty, and soundness in this world and the next. (2) O You Whom sins do not harm and from Whom forgiveness does not diminish anything — grant me that which will not harm You, and give me that which will not diminish You. Our Lord, pour upon us patience and cause us to die as Muslims. You are our Protector in this world and the next; cause me to die as a Muslim and join me with the righteous. You are our Protector, so forgive us and have mercy upon us, and You are the Best of forgivers. And write for us good in this world and in the Hereafter — indeed, we have turned to You in repentance. Our Lord, upon You we rely, to You we turn in repentance, and to You is the final return. Our Lord, make us not a trial for the wrongdoing people. Our Lord, make us not a trial for those who disbelieve, and forgive us, our Lord — indeed, You are the Mighty, the Wise. Our Lord, forgive us our sins and our excesses in our affairs, make firm our feet, and grant us victory over the disbelieving people. Our Lord, forgive us and our brothers who preceded us in faith, and place not in our hearts any rancor toward those who believe — our Lord, indeed You are Kind, Merciful. Our Lord, grant us from Yourself mercy and prepare for us from our affair right guidance. Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the chastisement of the Fire. Our Lord, indeed we have heard a caller calling to faith — to His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {«إنك لا تخلف الميعاد»} [آل عمران/ 194] — Our Lord, do not take us to task if we forget or err. Our Lord, to the end of the surah. (3) My Lord, forgive me and my parents, and have mercy upon them as they raised me when I was small; and forgive the believing men and the believing women, and the Muslim men and the Muslim women, the living among them and the dead. (4) My Lord, forgive, have mercy, and overlook what You know — and You are the Most Exalted, the Most Generous, the Best of the merciful, and the Best of the forgivers. And indeed, to God we belong and to Him we return; and there is no might and no power except through God, the Exalted, the Magnificent; and God suffices us, and He is the Best Disposer of affairs. And may God send blessings upon Muhammad, the Seal of the Prophets, and upon his family and his companions, and grant them abundant peace. (5)", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "section_title_ar": "Section 252", "section_title_en": "Section 252 — Supplications for Morning and Evening: Comprehensive Prayers of the Prophet (ﷺ)", "section_index": 252, "anchors": "- Root: لهم (l-h-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of swallowing/ingesting (iltihām); from this derives the sense of something being cast directly into the innermost recess of the heart (al-rawʿ).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الإلهام: إلقاء الشيء في الروع\" — ilhām is the casting of a thing into the innermost consciousness, specifically from God or the higher assembly (al-malaʾ al-aʿlā). It is that which the Prophet (ﷺ) called \"the touch of the angel\" (limat al-malak) and \"the breath of the Holy Spirit in my innermost heart\" (nafth rūḥ al-qudus fī rawʿī).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"ألهمه الله الخير: ألقاه في روعه\" — God inspired him with good: He cast it into his innermost consciousness. Metaphorical (majāz): A horse that \"swallows the ground\" (yaltaḥimu al-arḍ) in swiftness; thus ilhām is the swift, direct ingress of divine guidance into the soul without intermediary effort.\n- Root: حمد (ḥ-m-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The root denotes praise arising from recognition of voluntary excellence and beneficence; al-ḥamd is commendation of the beloved for their attributes and acts of goodness.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Praise (ḥamd) is the acknowledgment of beneficence (niʿmah) with reverence and love; it is distinguished from mere thanks (shukr) in that it is directed to the essence and attributes of the praised one, not solely to the benefit received.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"أحمد الله تعالى بجميع محامده\" — I praise God with all His praiseworthy attributes. Metaphorical: \"أحمدت صنيعه\" — I found his deed praiseworthy; thus the tongue's praise must be matched by the heart's recognition of the praised one's perfection.\n- Root: غفر (gh-f-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The root denotes covering and shielding; al-mighfar is the helmet that protects the head in battle.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الغفر: إلباس ما يصونه عن الدنس\" — Forgiveness is the clothing of that which shields from filth. God's forgiveness (maghfirah) is His shielding of the servant from the touch of chastisement, covering the sin so that it is as though it never were.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"اللهم غفرًا\" — O God, forgive. Metaphorical: The she-beasts that \"did not forgive\" their heedlessness (lam taghfir la-hā ghaflātuhā) — i.e., they did not shield their young from destruction; thus forgiveness is active protection, not mere erasure.\n- Root: نفس (n-f-s)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The self, the soul; that which breathes and has vital spirit; also used for the very essence of a thing.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"النفس: الروح\" — the soul is the spirit; and in God's saying {«ويحذركم الله نفسه»} [آل عمران/ 28], \"His Self\" means His very essence (dhāt), which — though grammatically expressed as an annexation implying distinction — is in reality identical, with no multiplicity in the Divine Essence.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"شيء نفيس\" — a precious thing. Metaphorical: \"دفق نفسه\" — he poured out his blood/life; thus nafs is the seat of life, passion, and moral responsibility.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الدعاء والخبر (The Chapter of Supplication and Assertion) — Supplications (duʿāʾ) are grammatically constructed as optative sentences (inshāʾ ṭalabī) using the imperative (rabbighfir), the jussive (lā tuʾākhidhnā), and the vocative (rabbanā), yet they may embed assertive clauses (khabar) of praise (al-ḥamdu lillāh) and attestation (lā ilāha illā anta). The periodic structure of these prayers alternates between direct address to God (munādāh) and self-referential confession, requiring the translator to preserve the vocative force of \"O God\" and \"Our Lord\" without flattening into mere description.", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the journey of the soul, death, and the Hereafter, from 'On Invocations and Supplications'", "badge": "Afterlife"}, {"arabic": "وإذا قال عليك توكلنا وإليك أنبنا وإليك المصير ولم يكن حاله التوكل والإنابة كان حاكيا وإذا قال ولنصبرن على ما آذيتمونا فليكن حاله الصبر أو العزيمة عليه حتى يجد حلاوة التلاوة فإن لم يكن بهذه الصفات ولم يتردد قلبه بين هذه الحالات كان حظه من التلاوة حركة اللسان مع صريح اللعن على نفسه في قوله تعالى إلا لعنة الله على الظالمين وفي قوله تعالى كبر مقتا عند الله أن تقولوا ما لا تفعلون وفي قوله عز وجل وهم في غفلة معرضون وفي قوله فأعرض عمن تولى عن ذكرنا ولم يرد إلا الحياة الدنيا وفي قوله تعالى ومن لم", "english": "And at the mention of God, His attributes, and His names, he bows low in humility before His majesty and in apprehension of His greatness. And at the mention of the disbelievers' sayings — those things impossible for God, Mighty and Majestic, such as their attributing to Him a son or a consort — he lowers his voice and inwardly recoils in shame at the ugliness of their speech. And at the description of Paradise, his innermost being surges forth with longing for it. And at the description of the Fire, his limbs tremble in fear of it. For when the Messenger of God, peace be upon him, said to Ibn Mas'ud, \"Recite to me,\" he said: \"I began reciting Surah al-Nisa'. When I reached {فكيف إذا جئنا من كل أمة بشهيد وجئنا بك على هؤلاء شهيدا} [How then shall it be when We bring from every nation a witness, and We bring you as a witness against these?] (4:41), I saw his two eyes overflowing with tears. He then said to me: 'That is enough for you now.'\" And this was because the witnessing of that very state had wholly overwhelmed his heart.", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "section_title_ar": "Section 230", "section_title_en": "The States of the Heart During Qur'anic Recitation — The Condition of the True Recieter", "section_index": 230, "anchors": "- Root: وجل (w-j-l)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root meaning of trembling fear, trepidation of the heart\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف\" — the inward apprehension of fear; cited in {إنما المؤمنون الذين إذا ذكر الله وجلت قلوبهم}\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"رجل وجل، وقوم وجال\" — a man fearful, a people fearful; the state of the heart's trembling before divine majesty\n- Root: وصف (w-ṣ-f)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Describing a thing by its attributes and qualities\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوصف: ذكر الشيء بحليته ونعته\" — description is the mention of a thing by its adornment and attribute; may be true or false\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical: \"وجهها يصف الحسن\" — metaphorical usage where the face itself \"describes\" beauty; likewise, the tongue may \"describe\" falsehood, as in {ولا تقولوا لما تصف ألسنتكم الكذب}\n- Root: وفي (w-f-y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Completeness, fulfillment, reaching full measure\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوافي: الذي بلغ التمام\" — that which attains completion; \"أوفى: إذا تمم العهد ولم ينقض حفظه\" — fulfilled the covenant without breach\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"درهم واف\" — a full-weight dirham; Metaphorical: \"أوفى على المائة إذا زاد عليها\" — surpassed the hundred\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The separation between the governing preposition and its object by intervening clauses, as in \"فلما بلغت {فكيف إذا جئنا...}\" where the temporal clause governs the narrative sequence", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "بالتقوى وغيره ومن هذا النوع قوله عز وجل حتى تؤمنوا بالله وحده إلا قول إبراهيم لأبيه الآية ومنها المبهم وهو اللفظ المشترك بين معن من كلمة أو حرف أما الكلمة فكالشيء والقرين والأمة والروح ونظائرها قال الله تعالى ضرب الله مثلا عبدا مملوكا لا يقدر على شيء أراد به النفقة مما رزق وقوله عز وجل وضرب الله مثلا رجلين أحدهما أبكم لا يقدر على شيء أي الأمر بالعدل والاستقامة وقوله عز وجل فإن اتبعتني فلا تسألني عن شيء أراد به من صفات الربوبية وهو العلوم التي لا يحل السؤال عنها حتى يبتدئ بها العارف في أوان الاستحقاق وقوله عز وجل أم خلقوا من غ", "english": "I say: The Prophet (peace be upon him) was asked about the means of deliverance from these trials, and he said: \"The Book of Allah — act by what is in it, for it is that which delivers one from them.\" The questioner repeated this three times, and he (peace be upon him) said three times: \"Learn the Book of Allah, Mighty and Glorious, and act by what is in it, for in it is deliverance.\"", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "section_title_ar": "Section 233", "section_title_en": "The Book of the Etiquette of Recitation — Section 233: On Understanding the Meanings of the Qur'an and the Limits of Interpretation", "section_index": 233, "anchors": "- Root: ف-ه-م (f-h-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الفهم: هيئة للإنسان بها يتحقق معاني ما يحسن\" — comprehension as an inherent faculty by which one ascertains meanings\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الفهم: هيئة للإنسان بها يتحقق معاني ما يحسن... وأفهمته: إذا قلت له حتى تصوره\" — comprehension is a cognitive disposition; distinction between understanding (fahm) and making understood (ifhām)\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"تقول: من لم يؤت من سوء الفهم أتى من سوء الإفهام\" — literal usage; failure of understanding often stems from failure of communication\n- Root: ف-س-ر (f-s-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"وكل شيء يعرف به تفسير الشيء ومعناه، فهو تَفْسِرَتُه\" — that by which a thing's meaning is made known\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"التفسير قد يقال فيما يختص بمفردات الألفاظ وغريبها، وفيما يختص بالتأويل\" — tafsīr concerns lexical surface; taʾwīl concerns deeper meaning\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"هذا كلام يحتاج إلى فسر وتفسير\" — literal: exposition of what is obscure\n- Root: و-ج-ل (w-j-l)\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف\" — the sensing of fear; used of hearts trembling at divine mention\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"لو واجلت فلانا لوجلته: لغلبته في الوجل\" — literal sense of fear; metaphorical extension to overpowering in fear\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — the particle innamā restricts predication, essential for parsing the Prophet's saying \"innamā al-aʿmālu bi-l-niyyāt\" and analogous restrictive formulations in the ḥadīth cited herein", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Insight"}], "7": [{"arabic": "قال الله تعالى {عسى الله أن يجعل بينكم وبين الذين عاديتم منهم مودة} وقال عليه السلام أحبب حبيبك هونا ما عسى أن يكون بغيضك يوما ما وأبغض بغيضك هونا ما عسى أن يكون حبيبك يوما ما (1) وقال عمر رضي الله عنه لا يكن حبك كلفا ولا بغضك تلفا وهو أن تحب تلف صاحبك مع هلاكك الحق السادس الدعاء للأخ في حياته وبعد مماته بكل ما يحبه لنفسه ولأهله وكل متعلق به فتدعو له كما تدعو لنفسك ولا تفرق بين نفسك وبينه فإن دعاءك له دعاء لنفسك على التحقيق فقد قال صلى الله عليه وسلم إذا دعا الرجل لأخيه في ظهر الغيب قال الملك ولك مثل ذل", "english": "Abū Sulaymān al-Dārānī said to Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Ḥawārī: \"If you take a brother in this age, do not reproach him for what you dislike, for you cannot be secure from seeing in his response to you something worse than the first [offense].\" He said: \"So I tried it, and I found it to be so.\"", "book_title": "Duties of Brotherhood", "section_title_ar": "Section 426", "section_title_en": "Section 426 — On the Rights of Brotherhood: Forbearance, Moderation in Love and Hate, and Supplication for the Brother in Life and After Death", "section_index": 426, "anchors": "- Root: شعث (sha-ʿatha)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Dishevelment, disorder of the hair; a state of being unkempt and scattered.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The condition of being disheveled or disordered, used metaphorically for the scattered, imperfect state of human affairs.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for unkempt hair; metaphorical for the flawed, rough edges of a person's character that require forbearance.\n- Root: وقع (wa-qa-ʿa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To fall, to occur, to befall; a falling into calamity.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-Wāqiʿah is not said except of severity and misfortune; most Quranic occurrences of \"waqaʿa\" pertain to chastisement and hardships.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: to fall to the ground. Metaphorical: to fall into slander or backbiting (al-waqīʿah), i.e., the utterance of evil against another.\n- Root: وفي (wa-fā)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To fulfill, to complete, to be complete and whole.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-Wāfī: that which has reached completion. Awfā bi-ʿahdihi: to complete the covenant and not break its observance.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: a full dirham, a full measure. Metaphorical: to complete one's life term; al-wafāʾ as the perfection of loyalty.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The permissibility of interposing elements between a preposition and its object when the intervening phrase is semantically complete, allowing for rhetorical emphasis and rhythmic balance in periodic constructions.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Duties of Brotherhood'", "badge": "Insight"}], "10": [{"arabic": "وقد قال الله تعالى يا أيها الذين آمنوا أنفقوا من طيبات ما كسبتم ومما أخرجنا لكم من الأرض ولا تيمموا الخبيث منه تنفقون ولستم بآخذيه إلا أن تغمضوا فيه أي لا تأخذوه إلا مع كراهية وحياء وهو معنى الإغماض فلا تؤثروا به ربكم وفي الخبر سبق درهم مائة ألف درهم (3) وذلك بأن يخرجه الإنسان وهو من أحل ماله وأجوده فيصدر ذلك عن الرضا والفرح بالبذل وقد يخرج مائة ألف درهم مما يكره من ماله فيدل ذلك على أنه ليس يؤثر الله عز وجل بشيء مما يحبه وبذلك ذم الله تعالى قوما جعلوا لله ما يكرهون فقال تعال", "english": "The heart is not treated save with the compound electuary (maʿjūn) of knowledge and works. And this condition among the conditions of almsgiving runs in the same course as humility (al-khushūʿ) runs in the prayer. This is established by his saying — may Allah bless him and grant him peace: \"A man has nothing of his prayer save that of which he was conscious.\" And this is like his saying — may Allah bless him and grant him peace: \"Allah does not accept the charity of the one who bestows it with reproach (al-mannān).\" And like His saying — Exalted is He: {«لا تبطلوا صدقاتكم بالمن والأذى»} (\"Do not nullify your charities by reproach and injury\"). As for the legal opinion (fatwā) of the jurist that the alms fall in their proper place and that one's liability is discharged without this condition — that is another discussion, and we have already pointed to its meaning in the Book of Prayer.", "book_title": "Duties of Brotherhood", "section_title_ar": "Section 175", "section_title_en": "The Inner Conditions of Charity — Section 175 (From The Revival of the Religious Sciences, Book of the Mysteries of Almsgiving)", "section_index": 175, "anchors": "- Root: قلب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"To turn, overturn, transform a thing from one state to another; to rotate, to flip\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — the heart is so named because of its constant turning and transformation between states\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه\" (to turn a thing from its face). Metaphorical: \"رجل قلب حول: يقلب الأمور ويحتال\" — one who turns matters over and manages them; \"قلبوا لك الأمور\" (they turned matters against you)\n- Root: وجل (w-j-l)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Fear, dread, apprehension that strikes the heart\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف\" — the sensing of fear; cited in {«إنما المؤمنون الذين إذا ذكر الله وجلت قلوبهم»}\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"رجل وجل، وقوم وجال\" — a fearful man, a fearful people; \"وفي قلبه وجل\" — in his heart is dread\n- Root: عجب (ʿ-j-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Wonder, amazement; self-admiration, vanity\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Self-admiration (al-ʿujb) is a destructive spiritual ailment that nullifies deeds\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: wonder at something extraordinary. Metaphorical: self-conceit regarding one's own acts of obedience\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction & Focused Predication) — governing the precise limitation of general categories (al-ṣifāt al-khāṣṣah within al-aṣnāf al-thamāniyyah) and the conditional structure of acceptance\n\n---\n\n##", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Duties of Brotherhood'", "badge": "Insight"}], "13": [{"arabic": "وقد قال الله تعالى يا أيها الذين آمنوا أنفقوا من طيبات ما كسبتم ومما أخرجنا لكم من الأرض ولا تيمموا الخبيث منه تنفقون ولستم بآخذيه إلا أن تغمضوا فيه أي لا تأخذوه إلا مع كراهية وحياء وهو معنى الإغماض فلا تؤثروا به ربكم وفي الخبر سبق درهم مائة ألف درهم (3) وذلك بأن يخرجه الإنسان وهو من أحل ماله وأجوده فيصدر ذلك عن الرضا والفرح بالبذل وقد يخرج مائة ألف درهم مما يكره من ماله فيدل ذلك على أنه ليس يؤثر الله عز وجل بشيء مما يحبه وبذلك ذم الله تعالى قوما جعلوا لله ما يكرهون فقال تعال", "english": "The heart is not treated save with the compound electuary (maʿjūn) of knowledge and works. And this condition among the conditions of almsgiving runs in the same course as humility (al-khushūʿ) runs in the prayer. This is established by his saying — may Allah bless him and grant him peace: \"A man has nothing of his prayer save that of which he was conscious.\" And this is like his saying — may Allah bless him and grant him peace: \"Allah does not accept the charity of the one who bestows it with reproach (al-mannān).\" And like His saying — Exalted is He: {«لا تبطلوا صدقاتكم بالمن والأذى»} (\"Do not nullify your charities by reproach and injury\"). As for the legal opinion (fatwā) of the jurist that the alms fall in their proper place and that one's liability is discharged without this condition — that is another discussion, and we have already pointed to its meaning in the Book of Prayer.", "book_title": "Duties of Brotherhood", "section_title_ar": "Section 175", "section_title_en": "The Inner Conditions of Charity — Section 175 (From The Revival of the Religious Sciences, Book of the Mysteries of Almsgiving)", "section_index": 175, "anchors": "- Root: قلب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"To turn, overturn, transform a thing from one state to another; to rotate, to flip\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — the heart is so named because of its constant turning and transformation between states\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه\" (to turn a thing from its face). Metaphorical: \"رجل قلب حول: يقلب الأمور ويحتال\" — one who turns matters over and manages them; \"قلبوا لك الأمور\" (they turned matters against you)\n- Root: وجل (w-j-l)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Fear, dread, apprehension that strikes the heart\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف\" — the sensing of fear; cited in {«إنما المؤمنون الذين إذا ذكر الله وجلت قلوبهم»}\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"رجل وجل، وقوم وجال\" — a fearful man, a fearful people; \"وفي قلبه وجل\" — in his heart is dread\n- Root: عجب (ʿ-j-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Wonder, amazement; self-admiration, vanity\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Self-admiration (al-ʿujb) is a destructive spiritual ailment that nullifies deeds\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: wonder at something extraordinary. Metaphorical: self-conceit regarding one's own acts of obedience\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction & Focused Predication) — governing the precise limitation of general categories (al-ṣifāt al-khāṣṣah within al-aṣnāf al-thamāniyyah) and the conditional structure of acceptance\n\n---\n\n##", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Duties of Brotherhood'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "ولم يستقر في القلب ولم يحركه إلى التوبة والتدارك أولئك يئسوا من الآخرة كما يئس الكفار من أصحاب القبور وهذا هو معنى اسوداد القلب بالذنوب كما نطق به القرآن والسنة قال ميمون بن مهران إذا أذنب العبد ذنبا نكت في قلبه نكته سوداء فإذا هو نزع وتاب صقل وإن عاد زيد فيها حتى يعلو قلبه فهو الران وقد قال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قلب المؤمن أجرد فيه سراج يزهر وقلب الكافر أسود منكوس (2) حديث القلوب أربعة قلب أجرد فيه سراج يزهر الحديث أخرجه أحمد والطبراني في الصغير من حديث أبي سعيد الخدري وقد تقدم فمثل الإيمان فيه كمثل البقلة يمدها الماء الطيب ومثل النفاق فيه ك", "english": "As for the praiseworthy effects that we have mentioned, they increase the mirror of the heart in clarity (jalā'), radiance (ishrāq), light (nūr), and brilliance (ḍiyā'), until the clear truth (jalīyat al-ḥaqq) gleams within it and the reality of the sought-after matter in religion is unveiled in it. And it is to such a heart that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, pointed when he said: \"When God desires good for a servant, He appoints for him an admonisher from his own heart.\" (1) The hadith: \"Whoever has from his heart an admonisher, upon him is from God a protector\" — I have not found for it a source (aṣl).", "book_title": "Disciplining the Soul", "section_title_ar": "Section 582", "section_title_en": "The Heart as a Mirror: The Effects of Virtues and Vices upon Spiritual Perception", "section_index": 582, "anchors": "- Root: قلب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To turn over, to overturn, to transform from one state to another; the heart as that which is constantly fluctuating and turning between states.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — The heart is that which is perpetually turned about, and its rectitude or corruption depends upon the direction of its turning.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): physical turning over. Metaphorical (Majaz): \"قلب المعلم الصبيان: صرفهم إلى بيوتهم\" — the turning of a thing toward its proper end. Here, the heart is a mirror (مرآة) turned toward either the light of truth or the darkness of sin.\n- Root: رين (r-y-n)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Rust, tarnish, or filth that overcomes a polished surface, veiling its original brightness.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The covering of the heart by accumulated sin, such that it becomes rusted over and incapable of receiving the light of truth.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the tarnishing of a blade or mirror. Metaphorical: the veiling of the heart's perceptive faculty by the accumulation of transgressions, as in {«كلا بل ران على قلوبهم ما كانوا يكسبون»} (The Mutaffifin: 14).\n- Root: طبع (t-b-')\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To stamp, to seal, to impress upon; the imprinting of a seal that renders the surface impermeable to further impression.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The sealing of the heart by God as a consequence of persistent sin, rendering it deaf to admonition and blind to truth.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the physical stamping of a seal. Metaphorical: the divine sealing of the heart as a just consequence of willful persistence in transgression.\n- Root: ذكر (dh-k-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Remembrance, recollection, mindfulness; the opposite of forgetfulness (نسيان).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The presence of the thing remembered in the mind; the highest form being the remembrance of God which brings tranquility to the heart.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: verbal invocation. Metaphorical: the state of spiritual presence and awareness that polishes the heart's mirror and unveils the reality of truth.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The syntactic connection between cause and effect, as in the verse {«واتقوا الله واسمعوا»}, where hearing (spiritual perception) is grammatically and semantically linked to piety (تقوى), just as the sealing of the heart (طبع) is linked to the accumulation of sins (ذنوب).", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Disciplining the Soul'", "badge": "Hadith"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 400, 3572], [2, 3572, 5325], [3, 5325, 7652], [4, 7652, 8459], [5, 8459, 10957], [6, 10957, 12919], [7, 12919, 15502], [8, 15502, 18654], [9, 18654, 20423], [10, 20423, 22161], [11, 22161, 24441], [12, 24441, 25667], [13, 25667, 27560], [14, 27560, 28677], [15, 28677, 31147], [16, 31147, 32217], [17, 32217, 33613], [18, 33613, 35816], [19, 35816, 37879], [20, 37879, 40648], [21, 40648, 41331], [22, 41331, 43627], [23, 43627, 45163], [24, 45163, 46637], [25, 46637, 47320], [26, 47320, 48561], [27, 48561, 50221], [28, 50221, 51785], [29, 51785, 52561], [30, 52561, 54454], [31, 54454, 57591], [32, 57591, 59887], [33, 59887, 61857], [34, 61857, 63595], [35, 63595, 65875], [36, 65875, 67519], [37, 67519, 68884], [38, 68884, 70795], [39, 70795, 72905], [40, 72905, 74971], [41, 74971, 76957], [42, 76957, 78043], [43, 78043, 79781], [44, 79781, 81022], [45, 81022, 82092], [46, 82092, 83038], [47, 83038, 85384], [48, 85384, 87469]], "2": [[1, 400, 1101], [2, 1101, 3745], [3, 3745, 6325], [4, 6325, 7281], [5, 7281, 9944], [6, 9944, 13815], [7, 13815, 15631], [8, 15631, 17893], [9, 17893, 20665], [10, 20665, 23508], [11, 23508, 26009], [12, 26009, 26805], [13, 26805, 28876]], "3": [[1, 400, 925], [2, 925, 2551], [3, 2551, 4623], [4, 4623, 6370], [5, 6370, 8285], [6, 8285, 9334], [7, 9334, 11091], [8, 11091, 12350], [9, 12350, 13793], [10, 13793, 15223], [11, 15223, 16167], [12, 16167, 17924], [13, 17924, 19184]], "4": [[1, 400, 1290], [2, 1290, 2961], [3, 2961, 4051], [4, 4051, 5722], [5, 5722, 7175], [6, 7175, 8955], [7, 8955, 11661], [8,